{"name":"Porcelain Skin","hex":"#ffe7eb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"porcelain skin","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["smooth skin"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porcelain_skin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Porcelain","blocks":[{"text":"Porcelain, also called china, is a ceramic material made by heating raw materials, generally including kaolinite, in a kiln to temperatures between 1,200 and 1,400 °C. The greater strength and translucence of porcelain, relative to other types of pottery, arise mainly from vitrification and the formation of the mineral mullite within the body at these high temperatures. End applications include tableware, decorative ware such as figurines, and products in technology and industry such as electrical insulators and laboratory ware."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/%E6%B1%9D%E7%AA%AF_%E9%9D%92%E7%93%B7%E8%86%BD%E7%93%B6.png/330px-%E6%B1%9D%E7%AA%AF_%E9%9D%92%E7%93%B7%E8%86%BD%E7%93%B6.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porcelain","wikidata":"Q130693"},{"title":"Skin","blocks":[{"text":"Skin is the layer of usually soft, flexible outer tissue covering the body of a vertebrate animal, with three main functions: protection, regulation, and sensation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Elephant_skin_%283689577529%29.jpg/330px-Elephant_skin_%283689577529%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skin","wikidata":"Q1074"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Allegorie_van_de_herfst_-_onbekend_-_KU_Leuven_Kunstpatrimonium_-_SPK379.jpg/120px-Allegorie_van_de_herfst_-_onbekend_-_KU_Leuven_Kunstpatrimonium_-_SPK379.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum